<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Volgobal 204     unloading   bran wheat	1,939     Europe</p>
<p>Omsky 138	  unloading   wheat	     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Auk		  arrived     corn	     23,002     U.S.</p>
<p>				     wheat	    18,900</p>
<p>				     sunflower meal  5,400</p>
<p>				     bran wheat	5,008</p>
<p>Kustenay	   13/5	  sunflower meal  2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Matusenko	  13/5	  maize grits     n/a	 Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Sun	20/5	  wheat	    53,650     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   8,190</p>
<p>Belle		20/5	  soya	     22,600     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   5,100</p>
<p>				     corn screening  7,000</p>
<p>Europa	     26/5	  corn	     20,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	   20,600</p>
<p>				     sunflower meal  6,000</p>
<p>Gencis K	    2/6	  gluten feed     8,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten meal     3,800</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   8,000</p>
<p>				     soya	     17,000</p>
<p>				     corn screening  6,000</p>
<p>				     wheat	     2,000</p>
